NEARS-2950 — AC5: Cross-store isolation (pre-existing ownership check, both surfaces)

== API surface ==
Vendor B = ecomarket@demo.com (vendor_id=19->store_id=19), token via
POST /api/v1/auth/vendor/login. Vendor B attempts to edit Vendor A's
(store_id=2) order 92991 via PUT /api/v1/vendor/update-order-amount:

$ curl -X PUT $BASE -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN_B" -H "vendorType: owner" -d "order_id=92991&order_amount=1"
{"errors":[{"code":"order","message":"Order not found"}]}
HTTP:403
DB check: orders.id=92991 order_amount still 999.00, store_id=2 (untouched).

== Web surface ==
Vendor B (id=20, countryfair@demo.com, store_id=23) attempts to edit Vendor
A's (store_id=2) order 93003 via the real
POST vendor-panel/order/update-order-amount route (full kernel dispatch,
session+CSRF, per ac3-ac4-web-panel.log method):

HTTP 302 -> http://localhost
Toastr: {"type":"error","message":"Order not found"}
DB order 93003: order_amount 999.00 -> 999.00 (unchanged)

Verdict: PASS — ownership check (`Order::where('store_id', Helpers::get_store_id())`
on web, `$order->store_id != $vendor_store->id` on API) rejects cross-store
edits ahead of/alongside the new NEARS-2950 status/prescription gate, on both
surfaces, confirmed live.
